Missing sysvar validation  
In the `release` function, the program does not verify that the `instructions_sysvar_info` account is the actual Solana instructions sysvar (it only checks the parsed inner instruction’s program ID). An attacker can substitute a fabricated account that mimics the sysvar layout and pass a forged ed25519 attestation, allowing unauthorized token releases. The missing check is:  
```rust
if instructions_sysvar_info.key != &solana_sdk::sysvar::instructions::ID {
    return Err(BridgeError::WrongSysvar.into());
}
``` (or the equivalent `instructions1` ID depending on the sysvar version).
